Keep one Call-ID and an increasing CSeq for the third-party REGISTERs.

Every third-party REGISTER of ims_isc got a new Call-ID and CSeq 10 from
tm, so an AS saw each re-registration and de-registration of an IMPU as
an unrelated registration. RFC 3261 10.2 says a UA SHOULD use the same
Call-ID for all its registrations to a registrar, with CSeq increasing
by one.

Keep a Call-ID and a CSeq counter per public identity and AS, in shared
memory, and give them to t_request(). The slot of the entry stays
locked until the request is sent, so the CSeqs of a Call-ID leave in
order. A de-registration ends the sequence, so the next registration
starts a new Call-ID; the state is also lost on a restart, which does
the same.

